 4. ☔️ Kalshi&#x27;s forecast: More weather wagers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Kalshi is partnering with the owner of the Weather Channel and Weather.com to exchange data on climate predictions and outcomes .

 The big picture: Kalshi is looking to beef up the weather predictions component of its exchange, allowing users to risk money on precipitation and temperatures.

 The Weather Co. will provide data that will serve as outcome verification for Kalshi traders. And the Weather Channel app and site will incorporate Kalshi prediction market insights. By the numbers: Kalshi said it's "pacing toward $1.1 billion in annualized volume as traders look to hedge weather risks or trade on shifting climate trends."

 💭 Nathan's thought bubble: Prediction markets can serve as a hedging opportunity for businesses that are greatly affected by the weather — but the question is whether the societal benefits of hedging will outweigh the risks of users losing money on frivolous trades.

 
 
